Here is a complete, precise account of how breadcrumbs are rendered and how each of the requested symbols is used.

---

## 1. Breadcrumb Rendering Pipeline

### Entry point: `GlobalBreadcrumbShell`

**File:** `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/apps/desktop/src/components/navigation/navigation-shell.tsx` (line 211)

This is the top-level component that renders the breadcrumb bar globally. It reads the active tab's `breadcrumbStack` from `useActiveTabState()` and converts it:

```tsx
const derivedHeader = useMemo(
  () => buildDerivedHeader(currentNavigationState?.breadcrumbStack, workspaces),
  [currentNavigationState?.breadcrumbStack, workspaces]
);
```

`buildDerivedHeader` (same file, line 84) converts `BreadcrumbStackItem[]` to segments. The root item with `descriptorId === "workspace"` is stripped out and used as the `workspace` prop; the remaining items become `DesktopBreadcrumbSegment[]` via `mapStackItemToSegment`.

**`mapStackItemToSegment`** (line 71) is where `BreadcrumbStackItem` fields map to segment fields:
```tsx
function mapStackItemToSegment(item: BreadcrumbStackItem): DesktopBreadcrumbSegment {
  return {
    id: item.id,
    label: item.label,         // BreadcrumbStackItem.label -> segment.label
    href: item.target?.canonicalUrl ?? "#",  // .target -> .href
    icon: item.icon,           // BreadcrumbStackItem.icon -> segment.icon
    descriptorId: item.descriptorId,
    meta: item.meta,
  };
}
```

The resolved `workspace` + `segments` are passed to `<DesktopBreadcrumbBar>`.

---

### Core rendering: `DesktopBreadcrumbBar`

**File:** `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/apps/desktop/src/components/navigation/desktop-breadcrumb-bar.tsx`

This renders the `<header>` containing the breadcrumb `<nav>`. The key loop is at line 284:

```tsx
{allSegments.map((segment, index) => {
  const isCurrent = index === allSegments.length - 1;
  return (
    <div key={key} className="flex items-center gap-1">
      {index > 0 ? <ChevronRight ... /> : null}
      {renderDropdown(segment, isCurrent, ...)}
    </div>
  );
})}
```

**`renderSegmentButton`** (line 188) renders each breadcrumb button:
- `segment.icon` is passed to `<IconDisplay icon={segment.icon} .../>` for the icon
- `segment.label` is rendered as `<span>{segment.label}</span>`
- `segment.target` is used indirectly via `segment.href` (which was set from `target.canonicalUrl`)
- On click, `popToBreadcrumb(stackIndex)` or `navigateWithTab(segment)` is called; the latter calls `openPath(segment.href, { descriptorId: ..., title: segment.label, icon: segment.icon, ... })`

**`renderDropdown`** (line 223) wraps each segment button in a `<BreadcrumbDropdown>` populated by `resolvePageIndexBranch(...)`.

---

### Dropdown rendering: `BreadcrumbDropdown`

**File:** `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/apps/desktop/src/components/navigation/breadcrumb-dropdown.tsx`

Renders a hover-activated popover. Each `BreadcrumbDropdownItem` is rendered as a `<Button>`:
- `item.icon` -> `<IconDisplay icon={item.icon} .../>` (line 98)
- `item.label` -> `<span>{item.label}</span>` (line 104)
- `item.description` -> rendered as a subtitle (line 107)
- `item.isActive` -> shows a `<Check>` icon (line 113)

---

## 2. How `BreadcrumbStackItem.icon`, `.label`, `.target` Are Used

**Type definition:** `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/apps/desktop/src/navigation/navigation-meta.ts` (line 152)

- **`.label`** - Rendered as the visible text of the breadcrumb button (`<span>{segment.label}</span>` in `desktop-breadcrumb-bar.tsx` line 219). Also used as the tab title when navigating.
- **`.icon`** - Rendered via `<IconDisplay icon={segment.icon} .../>` in `renderSegmentButton` (line 214). If absent on a `BreadcrumbStackItem`, it is filled in by `getDescriptorIcon(item.descriptorId)` at creation time (see below).
- **`.target`** - Contains a `ViewTarget` with `canonicalUrl`. It becomes `segment.href` via `mapStackItemToSegment` → used as the navigation URL in `popToBreadcrumb` / `openPath`.

---

## 3. How `getDescriptorIcon(descriptorId)` Is Called

