## 4. How `VirtualPageIndexNode` and Its `descriptorId` Are Used

**Type definition:** `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/apps/desktop/src/navigation/navigation-meta.ts` (line 173)

```ts
export interface VirtualPageIndexNode {
  id: string;
  /** References a BreadcrumbItemDescriptor.id */
  descriptorId: string;   // <-- references e.g. "workspace", "workspace-section:chat"
  label: string;
  icon?: IconData;
  parentId?: string;
  order: number;
  isContainer?: boolean;
  target?: ViewTarget;
  childSource?: { type: ...; workspaceId?: string; pageSlug?: string; };
  contentRef?: { pageSlug: string; blockId?: string; };
}
```

**Creation in `page-index.ts`:** `/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/apps/desktop/src/navigation/page-index.ts`

`createWorkspaceRootNode` (line 213) creates a node with `descriptorId: "workspace"`. `createStaticWorkspaceIndexNodes` (line 227) creates section children where `descriptorId` is set to the section descriptor's `.id` (e.g. `"workspace-section:chat"`):

```ts
const sectionNodes = WORKSPACE_SECTION_DESCRIPTORS.map((section, index) => ({
  id: `${root.id}:${section.section}`,
  descriptorId: section.id,   // e.g. "workspace-section:chat"
  label: section.fallbackLabel,
  icon: section.icon,
  parentId: root.id,
  ...
}));
```

**Usage in `resolvePageIndexBranch`** (line 596): `VirtualPageIndexNode` is not directly iterated in the UI components found. The `descriptorId` from `DesktopBreadcrumbSegment` (which mirrors it) is used by `resolveSegmentDescriptorId` to dispatch which dropdown items to show. For example:
- `descriptorId === "workspace"` → shows workspace-switcher dropdown
- `descriptorId.startsWith("workspace-section:")` → shows workspace section navigation dropdown
- `descriptorId === "workspace-page"` → shows sibling page navigation dropdown
- `descriptorId.startsWith("settings")` → shows settings sections dropdown

**Rendering note:** `VirtualPageIndexNode` is purely a data model. The `page-section.tsx` sidebar component (`/Users/lxy/Documents/GitHub/LinXueyuanStdio/viben/apps/desktop/src/pages/apps/components/page-section.tsx`) renders pages from `PageConfig` (from the gateway), not from `VirtualPageIndexNode` directly. `VirtualPageIndexNode` nodes are constructed in `page-index.ts` but are used as an intermediate structure for building the navigation DAG — their `descriptorId` drives the dropdown dispatch logic in `resolvePageIndexBranch`, not any direct rendering loop.
